course: dictionary
lesson: 3551
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «I fell off my bike» uses fell as the past of fall, so you dropped down. «They felled the old oak» means they cut the tree down. Look at the clues around the word to decide.
explain: Ask what is happening in the sentence. Is someone falling, cutting, or describing a hill? When a number is used, like «the temperature fell by 5 degrees», fell means it went down, and in maths that is a subtraction. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Fell also appears in set phrases, which you learn as a whole. «Fell asleep» means began to sleep, «fell ill» means became sick, and «fell in love» means started to love someone. Do not translate each word on its own, because the phrase has its own meaning.
fact: Fell is the past of fall: fall, falls, fell, fallen, falling.
fact: As a verb, fell means to cut down a tree, or to knock someone down.
fact: A fell (UK noun) is a hill or high moor in the north of England, as in the Lake District fells.
fact: «Fell» can also be an old or poetry word meaning cruel or terrible.
fact: «At one fell swoop» means all at once.
exercise: Yesterday the apples «fell» from the tree. What does fell mean here? | Cruel and terrible | A high hill | *Dropped down | Cut down
exercise: The woodcutter «felled» the old oak. What does felled mean? | Painted green | *Cut down | Dropped down | Lost in the forest
exercise: The walkers climbed the fells in the Lake District. What is a fell? | A type of tree | *A high hill or moor | A kind of boat | A small lake
test: Mia «fell asleep» on the bus. What does fell asleep mean? | Fell off the seat | Woke up with a jump | *Began to sleep | Sang a quiet song
test: The price of bread «fell» by ten pence. Which word means the same as fell here? | Went up | Stayed the same | Ran away | *Went down
exam: «They dealt with the danger at one fell swoop.» What does at one fell swoop mean? | Very slowly | With a loud noise | Up on a hill | *All at once
